{#
  The end of every page's Markdown: the archive on a page that asked for one,
  what the page is filed under, what links to it, a post's neighbours, the
  conversation, where the comment and contact forms are, the feeds, then a
  heading and the site's link lists.

  `archiveMonths` is on the context only of a page whose front matter says
  `archive: true`: every published post as `{ month, posts }`, newest month
  first. Each post is a `label`, a `url`, a `date` (`YYYY-MM-DD`) and a
  `description` already on one line, written here in the shape a listing's
  Markdown has.

  `categories` and `tags` are a post's, each a `label` (the term as written)
  and the `url` of its archive. `backlinks` are the site's posts and pages
  that link to this one, newest first, each a `label`, a `url` and a `date`.
  This theme leaves them off a homepage that is a page, as its front page
  layout does; a site theme may print them there.
  `feeds` are the feeds the HTML head advertises, each a `label` (the feed's
  title), a `url`, a `format` (`RSS`, `Atom` or `JSON Feed`) and a `type`.
  `conversation` is on a post or page that has been answered: what
  `conversation.njk` draws, from the same reader, so nothing the HTML hides
  is in it. Its `rsvps`, `likes`, `boosts` and `mentions` are people, each a
  `label` and a `url` when there is one. Its `replies` are threaded as the
  HTML's are, each a `key`, `source`, `author` (a `label` and a `url`), `url`,
  `published`, `rsvp`, `text` (its words as Markdown) and its own `replies`,
  or a `withheld` placeholder with only `replies`. `nest` indents a reply
  under its list item. `commentForm` and `contactForm` are each the `url` of
  the form on the HTML page, printed as it is, since a form needs HTML;
  `commentForm` is absent while comments are closed. `webmention` is there
  when the site takes webmentions.
  `type` is `post`, `page` or `listing`; a listing's newer and older pages
  are written by the CMS above this, so only a post's `previous` and `next`
  are printed here.

  `byline` is a post's author, a `label` and the `url` of their archive.
  `navigation` is every item of every menu the site stores, each URL once,
  each a `label` and a `url`; `menus` has them by menu name, as the HTML
  does. `home`, `previous` and `next` are here too; the front matter carries
  them as well, for a Markdown browser.

  Each link is a line of its own, with its own words, so the same data can be
  written as a Gemini link line. Nothing is printed when there is nothing to
  link.
#}
{% macro named(person) %}{{ ("[" + (person.label | escapeMarkdown) + "](" + (person.url | markdownUrl) + ")") if person.url else (person.label | escapeMarkdown) }}{% endmacro %}
{% macro reply(entry) %}
{% if entry.withheld %}
- This comment is no longer shown.
{% else %}
- {{ named(entry.author) }}, {{ ("[" + (entry.published | date) + "](" + (entry.url | markdownUrl) + ")") if entry.url else (entry.published | date) }}{{ ", via webmention" if entry.source == "webmention" }}{{ ", via the fediverse" if entry.source == "activitypub" }}
{% if entry.rsvp %}

  {{ entry.rsvp.label | escapeMarkdown }}
{% endif %}
{% if entry.text %}

  {{ entry.text | nest(2) }}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% for child in entry.replies %}

  {{ reply(child) | trim | nest(2) }}
{% endfor %}
{% endmacro %}
{% for group in archiveMonths %}
## {{ group.month | escapeMarkdown }}

{% for entry in group.posts %}
- [{{ (((entry.date + " ") if entry.date) + entry.label) | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ entry.url | markdownUrl }}){{ (": " + entry.description) if entry.description }}
{% endfor %}

{% endfor %}
{% if categories.length or tags.length %}
## Filed under

{% for link in categories %}
- [Category: {{ link.label | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ link.url | markdownUrl }})
{% endfor %}
{% for link in tags %}
- [Tag: {{ link.label | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ link.url | markdownUrl }})
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if backlinks.length and not staticFrontPage %}
## Linked from

{% for entry in backlinks %}
- [{{ (((entry.date + " ") if entry.date) + entry.label) | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ entry.url | markdownUrl }})
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if type == "post" and (previous or next) %}
## More posts

{% if previous %}
- [Previous: {{ previous.label | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ previous.url | markdownUrl }})
{% endif %}
{% if next %}
- [Next: {{ next.label | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ next.url | markdownUrl }})
{% endif %}

{% endif %}
{% if conversation %}
{% for group in conversation.rsvps.concat([{ label: "Likes", people: conversation.likes }, { label: "Boosts", people: conversation.boosts }, { label: "Mentions", people: conversation.mentions }]) %}
{% if group.people.length %}
## {{ group.label | escapeMarkdown }} ({{ group.people.length }})

{% for person in group.people %}
- {{ named(person) }}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if conversation.replies.length %}
## {{ conversation.counts.replies | plural({ one: "One reply", other: "# replies" }, "en") }}

{% for entry in conversation.replies %}
{{ reply(entry) | trim }}

{% endfor %}
{% if not commentForm %}
Comments are closed.

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if commentForm %}
## Leave a comment

[Leave a comment on the web page]({{ commentForm.url }})

{% if webmention %}
Or reply from your own site and send a [webmention](https://indieweb.org/Webmention).

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if contactForm %}
## Send a message

[Send a message on the web page]({{ contactForm.url }})

{% endif %}
{% if feeds.length %}
## Feeds

{% for feed in feeds %}
- [{{ (feed.label + " (" + feed.format + ")") | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ feed.url | markdownUrl }})
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if byline or navigation.length %}
## {{ site.title | escapeMarkdown }}

{% if byline %}
[Written by {{ byline.label | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ byline.url | markdownUrl }})

{% endif %}
{% for item in navigation %}
- [{{ item.label | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ item.url | markdownUrl }})
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
